Let the shell close a window it was given a surface for.

auxiliaryDismissWidget reached RequestCloseLogicalWindow, which refused any
window that was not `auxiliary`. A window stops being auxiliary the moment the
shell hosts it in a surface of its own -- which is what happens to an incognito
window and to a tab dragged out into its own window, both of which arrive as
windowRole "browser" with an aura_win_<widget> surface. So exactly the windows
the shell draws a close button on were the ones it could not close, and the
call returned false with nothing happening.

The same check guarded the other end: a promoted window was erased without the
shell being told, so no destroyed event either.

Both now turn on whether the shell has ever been told the window exists, which
is true for an auxiliary window and stays true after it is promoted. The first
window is still left out -- the shell has always had it and is never told about
it, so it cannot ask to close it by accident.

The close itself was already right and is unchanged: the request reaches
OnCloseRequest on the platform window, the same path a title bar's close button
takes, so the tabs close in order, the session records them and the window is
torn down properly. The destroyed event follows from UnregisterLogicalWindow
once it has.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/ohos/ohos_native_window_registry.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/ohos/ohos_native_window_registry.cc
